<title>BELGIUM: EU clears AHOLD/Central Serveis control of Store 2000.</title>
<headline>EU clears AHOLD/Central Serveis control of Store 2000.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Tuesday it had cleared an operation under which Dutch company Koninklijke Ahold NV and Central Serveis Ciencies of Spain will acquire joint control of Spanish retail chain Store 2000 SA.</p>
<p>The Commission said in a statement that Store 2000, which has 11 supermarkets in Madrid, does not have a significant market share.</p>
<p>Its joint acquisition by Ahold, a Dutch supermarket group which has branches in Portugal, the United States, the Czech Republic and Poland, and Central Serveis would not therefore create a dominant position, it said.</p>
</text>
